    {
      "caption": "Circular motion needs a centre-seeking push",
      "duration_ms": 9000,
      "id": "s1",
      "narration": "A satellite stays on its circular path only because something keeps pulling it towards the centre. The blue arrow is that pull: it always points at the centre, no matter where the satellite is on its orbit.",
