    {
      "caption": "How big is the centre-seeking force",
      "duration_ms": 9000,
      "id": "s2",
      "narration": "The centre-seeking acceleration is v squared over r: spin twice as fast and it quadruples; double the radius and it halves. Multiply by the mass and you have the centripetal force, m v squared over r.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at_ms": 0,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "cx": 300,
            "cy": 300,
            "fill": "#1f7a3a",
            "id": "planet",
            "kind": "circle",
            "r": 28
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 1200,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "cx": 460,
            "cy": 300,
            "fill": "#b00020",
            "id": "sat",
            "kind": "circle",
            "r": 12
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 2400,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "fcent",
            "kind": "arrow",
            "stroke": "#b00020",
            "width": 4,
            "x1": 440,
            "x2": 345,
            "y1": 300,
            "y2": 300
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 3400,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "color": "#1f7a3a",
            "id": "accEq",
            "kind": "latex",
            "size": 44,
            "tex": "a = \\frac{v^2}{r}",
            "x": 560,
            "y": 190
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 4400,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "color": "#b00020",
            "id": "forceEq",
            "kind": "latex",
            "size": 44,
            "tex": "F = m\\frac{v^2}{r}",
            "x": 560,
            "y": 280
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 5600,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "scaleNote",
            "kind": "text",
            "size": 26,
            "text": "faster spin or tighter turn → bigger pull",
            "x": 120,
            "y": 440
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 6800,
          "do": "emphasize",
          "dur_ms": 900,
          "target": "fcent"
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 7800,
          "do": "caption",
          "text": "Centripetal force grows with speed squared, shrinks with radius"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "caption": "Gravity holds the Moon in orbit",
      "duration_ms": 9000,
      "id": "s3",
      "narration": "For the Moon, gravity itself supplies the centripetal force: F equals G M m over r squared. The same pull that weighs you on a bathroom scale keeps the Moon circling the Earth — every orbit is a continuous fall towards the centre.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at_ms": 0,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "cx": 480,
            "cy": 270,
            "fill": "#1a56db",
            "id": "earth",
            "kind": "circle",
            "r": 36
          }
        },
